WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.300
Pagewise. Find the page, not just the book.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.100
Search inside every page of your PDFs.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.800
Every passage that matches comes with its page number.

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.200
Click a page number, and the document opens right there, with your words highlighted.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:26.000
It works in any language, including Chinese, Japanese and Korean, even mixed in one search.

6
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.900
New files?

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.200
Apple's on-device model reads the first pages and fills in the catalogue entry.

8
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.300
Nothing leaves your Mac.

9
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:43.300
Scan one QR code, and your library is on your phone, anywhere, privately, through Tailscale.

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.800
And AI agents can search your books and cite the exact page, through MCP.

11
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.100
Pagewise for Mac.

12
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.600
Your library, searchable to the page.
